# Spring Boot Architecture Rules

## Layer Isolation
`@RestController` handles HTTP only: parse the incoming request, delegate to a `@Service`, and return the response. Zero business logic in controllers. If a controller method contains an `if` statement that is not about HTTP concerns, it belongs in the service layer.

## DTOs at the Boundary
The API layer uses Data Transfer Objects. In Java 21, prefer records:

```java
public record UserDto(
    @NotBlank String name,
    @Email String email
) {}
```

Entity types (`@Entity` classes) must never be returned from controllers or passed as method parameters across the service boundary. Map between entity and DTO using MapStruct.

## Service Layer Owns Transactions
`@Transactional` belongs on `@Service` methods. Never annotate controllers or repository implementations with `@Transactional`. The service is the transaction boundary.

## Read-Only Transactions
Annotate read-only service methods with `@Transactional(readOnly = true)`. This hint allows the database driver and Hibernate to apply optimizations (e.g., skip dirty checking, use read replicas).

```java
@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public UserDto findById(Long id) { ... }
```

## Repository Interfaces Only
Extend `JpaRepository<Entity, ID>` or `CrudRepository<Entity, ID>`. Do not inject `EntityManager` in application code unless you are writing complex dynamic JPQL that Spring Data cannot express. Custom query methods via `@Query` are fine.

## Validation at Entry
Validate all incoming DTOs with `@Valid` or `@Validated` on the controller parameter. Define constraints (`@NotBlank`, `@Email`, `@Size`, etc.) on the DTO fields, not on entity fields. Entities are internal; DTOs are the public contract.

```java
@PostMapping
public ResponseEntity<UserDto> create(@Valid @RequestBody UserDto dto) { ... }
```

## Global Exception Handling
Use `@ControllerAdvice` with `@ExceptionHandler` methods for all error responses. Never catch exceptions in individual controller methods just to convert them to HTTP responses — that is the adviser's job.

```java
@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
    @ExceptionHandler(EntityNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleNotFound(EntityNotFoundException ex) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
            .body(new ErrorResponse(ex.getMessage()));
    }
}
```

## No `@Autowired` on Fields
Use constructor injection exclusively. Immutable beans make tests easier and dependencies explicit. Lombok `@RequiredArgsConstructor` generates the constructor automatically:

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class UserService {
    private final UserRepository userRepository;
    private final UserMapper userMapper;
}
```

Field injection with `@Autowired` is forbidden.
